## Part I: The Story — Why Agent Anna Was Built to Run the Catalog

Every serious music run begins when the songs already carry weight before the pitch even starts. For **Martin Strayd (`STRAYD`)**, the foundation is a deep catalog of 70+ original songs, real room tension, melodies that stick after one listen, and a direct ownership model where listeners get the MP3 and cover sleeve straight from the source instead of renting a stream. Music played at **Kunda Cafe** brings its own grounded, lived-in pulse—distinct from the cafe itself—and a catalog of 70+ tracks is far too large to promote by accident or one-off posts.

A catalog that deep needs daily momentum, sharp positioning, and a tireless operator who knows every song's hook, mood, search keywords, and visual framing. That is why **Agent Anna** exists.

In this handbook, **Agent Anna** is not a passive chat box or a generic copy generator. She operates as DJ, artist manager, and campaign strategist for **Martin Strayd (`STRAYD`)**. She pulls external context and song notes kept outside `A1/v4` so the `v4` core stays lean, uses **Dahl** when deeper creative rewrites and chat synthesis are needed, frames every visual cue around **strictly realistic live-action cinematography (zero cartoon)**, shapes every draft to each platform's real space and search behavior, and stages everything under your **OK To Post** approval gate.

